  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 255 AM EDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nBroad troughing and its attendant cold front will continue \nmaking slow progress across northern Michigan through tonight \ninto Thursday, bringing a few rounds of showers and embedded \nthunderstorms along the way. For today through tonight, shower \ncoverage is expected to steadily increase as deeper moisture \nspreads overhead and becomes increasingly coupled with stronger \nupper-level support. The better focus for more widespread \nshowers/ thunderstorms gradually shifts southeast through the \nday, with the highest rainfall totals favored across northeast \nLower, particularly toward the Saginaw Bay region. Localized \nheavier rainfall remains possible with WPC continuing to \nhighlight mostly all of northern Lower Michigan for today. \nGuidance also continues to favor a little more forward progress \nwith the front on Thursday, allowing the better shower chances \nto gradually exit southeast through the afternoon. \n\nLooking beyond Thursday, overall forecast thinking remains \nlargely unchanged, with the larger-scale trough expected to \nbecome established across the Great Lakes through the weekend \ninto early next week. This should keep any meaningful heat \nsuppressed to our south while also maintaining periodic \nopportunities for showers as subtle waves rotate through the \nmean west to northwest flow. That said, there continues to be \nlittle indication of any prolonged stretch of wet weather, with \ndry periods likely separating any passing disturbances and \nperhaps cooler temperatures as well.",
